# Trivy ignore file — registry allow-list policy checks that do not apply to
# the digest-pinned upstream images used by this reusable Helm chart.
# Runtime hardening findings (UID/GID, capabilities,
# readOnlyRootFilesystem, seccomp, privilege escalation) are fixed in the
# templates, not ignored. The central trivy-fs gate targets CRITICAL,HIGH and
# there are zero CRITICAL/HIGH findings.

# KSV-0125: "Restrict container images to trusted registries".
# The trusted-registry allow-list is deployment policy, not a chart defect.
# Third-party images are pinned by immutable sha256 digest
# (quay.io/keycloak/keycloak, docker.io/library/postgres), which is a stronger
# guarantee than registry trust, and the first-party account-unification image
# repository is an operator-overridable value. Enforce registry trust via
# admission control at deploy time, not against the packaged chart defaults.
KSV-0125
